<title>USA: Sugar output 1997/98 in major nations - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sugar output 1997/98 in major nations - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department estimates, released Friday, of sugar production for 1997/98 in major nations, compared to 1996/97 (Mln tonnes):</p>
<p>    Nation	  1997/98  1996/97</p>
<p>    Mexico	    4.770    4.670</p>
<p>    United States   6.804    6.532</p>
<p>    Cuba		4.500    4.400</p>
<p>    Brazil	   14.800   14.650</p>
<p>    European Union 17.635   18.297</p>
<p>    FSU		 5.165    5.165</p>
<p>    Colombia	  2.045    2.044</p>
<p>    Poland	    1.900    2.497</p>
<p>    Russia	    1.800    1.750</p>
<p>    Ukraine	   2.850    2.900</p>
<p>    South Africa    2.500    2.408</p>
<p>    Turkey	    2.200    2.025</p>
<p>    China	     7.175    7.085</p>
<p>    India	    13.650   14.686</p>
<p>    Indonesia	 2.150    2.095</p>
<p>    Thailand	  6.360    6.255</p>
<p>    Philippines     1.800    1.800</p>
<p>    Australia	 5.650    5.491</p>
</text>
